<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<handout>
    <title>More Practice with Congruence and Divides</title>

    <page>
        <p>
            It will be important to both internalize the exact definitions, and
            have some intuition.
            This practice is to help with that!
        </p>

        <activity>
            <title>Defintions</title>

            <introduction>
                <p>
                    First, let's start with definitions!
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task workspace="1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        State the precise definition of divides below.
                        That is, complete the sentence a
                        <fillin characters="20"/> integer <m>a</m> divides an
                        integer <m>b</m> if
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task workspace="1in">
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        State the precise definition congruence below.
                        That is, complete the sentence for
                        <m>a,b \in <fillin characters="5"/></m> and
                        <m>m \in <fillin characters="5"/></m>, we say <m>a</m>
                        is congruent to <m>b</m> modulo <m>m</m> or (in
                        notation) <fillin characters="20"/> if
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </activity>

        <activity workspace=".3in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    Now let's practice doing the math! You can do it intuitively if you've got an idea, but then check
                    with the official defintion!
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task>
                <statement>
                   <p>
                    Determine if the following are true or false.
                    <ol>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m> 3\mid 12 </m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                          <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>12 \mid 3</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>7 \mid 50</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>5 \mid 0</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>0 \mid 5</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>-4 \mid 12</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>6\mid -18</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>1 \mid 9999999</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                      
                    </ol>
                   </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        For each of the following, determine if true or false.
                  

                    <ol>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>17 \equiv  5 \pmod{6}</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>23 \equiv  2 \pmod{6}</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>8 \equiv  -4 \pmod{6}</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>100 \equiv  1 \pmod{6}</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>-1 \equiv 6 \pmod{7}</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>

                        <li>
                            <p>
                                <m>45 \equiv 0 \pmod{9}</m>
                            </p>
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                      </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </activity>

        <activity workspace=".5in">
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    More advanced practice.
                </p>
            </introduction>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find all integers <m>n</m> such that <m>n\mid 15</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                       Find all integers <m>n</m> with <m>0\le n\le 100</m> such that <m>11\mid n</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find the smallest nonnegative integer <m>x</m> such that <m>47\equiv x\pmod{5}</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find all integers <m>x</m> such that
                        <m>x \equiv 1 \pmod{5}</m>.
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find all integers <m>x</m> such that
                        <m>3x\equiv 6 \pmod{9}</m> (or say that none exist).
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        Find all integers <m>x</m> such that
                        <m>5x\equiv 3 \pmod{7}</m> (or say that none exist).
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </activity>

        <activity workspace="1in">
            <title>For fun</title>
            
            <introduction>
                <p>
                    These problems are for people who want an additional challenge/more fun.
                </p>
            </introduction>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        For which integers <m>n</m> does <m>6\mid n</m> and <m>6\mid (n+15)</m>
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        What is the remainder when <m>2^{100}</m> is divided by 7? 
                        (Hint: find a pattern in powers of 2 mod 7.)
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        If you know <m>a \mid b</m>, what are 3 other divides expressions you could
                        say?
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>

            <task>
                <statement>
                    <p>
                        We saw in class, that if you take a type <m>1</m> integer and multiply 
                        with another type <m>1</m> integer the result is a type <m>1</m> integer. This
                        is equivalent to saying if <m>x\equiv 1 \pmod{3}\</m> and <m>y\equiv 1 \pmod{3}</m>,
                        then <m>xy\equiv 1 \pmod{3}</m>. So if we are multiplying <q>mod 3</q>, then <m>1 \cdot 1 = 1</m>.

                        What is <m>2\cdot 2</m> <q>mod 3</q>? Can you fill out a multiplication table for 3? What about 4? 
                        Do you see any patterns?
                    </p>
                </statement>
            </task>
        </activity>
    </page>
</handout>